The invariant `Valid()` fails on entry because `Append` has no precondition saying the object is valid on entry, so `cs` can be arbitrary (for example `cs = 10`). The fix is to add `requires Valid()`. I'll also add a hint for preservation, which needs `(data + [c])[..|data|] == data` to unfold `SumChars`.

```bash
cat > diagnosis.json <<'EOF'
{"spec_element": "requires",
 "proof_obligation": "initiation",
 "diagnosis": "Append lacks a precondition 'requires Valid()'. Without it, nothing relates cs to Hash(data) on entry (e.g. cs = 10, data arbitrary), so the loop invariant Valid() cannot be established at loop entry when i = 0. Adding requires Valid() to Append fixes initiation."}
EOF
python3 - <<'EOF'
p='program.dfy'
s=open(p).read()
s=s.replace("""        modifies this
        ensures Valid() && data == old(data) + d
""","""        requires Valid()
        modifies this
        ensures Valid() && data == old(data) + d
""")
s=s.replace("""            cs := (cs + d[i] as int) % 137;
            data := data + [d[i]];
""","""            ghost var oldData := data;
            cs := (cs + d[i] as int) % 137;
            data := data + [d[i]];
            assert data[..|data|-1] == oldData;
            assert SumChars(data) == d[i] as int + SumChars(oldData);
            assert d[..i+1] == d[..i] + [d[i]];
""")
open(p,'w').write(s)
EOF
sed -n 25,46p program.dfy</parameter>
```

